  "description": "Whose tail is this? Guess with Milo the bluebird, then find out what each tail can do: a lion's tail ends in a dark tuft like a paintbrush, a spider monkey's tail works like a third hand and even has lines like a fingerprint, and a giraffe's tail swats away buzzy flies.\nAn interactive animal guessing lesson for kids ages 2-6, with questions to answer, actions to copy, quick checks and a quiz at the end.\n\nThe Animated Zoo makes gentle, colorful videos for little learners. New videos every day! Made with care for ages 2-6. Every fact is checked against trusted sources and every script is reviewed for kid safety before publishing.",
